    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0063" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg63"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Sanford</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                            State</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 12, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch dated July 3 (No. 11) has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>I am quite content, under existing circumstances, with the disposition you
                    propose in that paper to make of the subject of passports, and I acquiesce very
                    cheerfully in the views which you take of the importance of vigilance in regard
                    to the movements of disaffected citizens of our own country travelling in
                    Europe.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry S. Sanford</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Brussels.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
